@allenporter was hoping you could have a look at this one. Perhaps some of the recent updates over the last few monthly releases has introduced this?

Hello, I encounter this kind of behaviour when opening a valve while another is still open. 
The first one is closed but the new one doesn't remain open and it seems to trigger a controller crash/recovery. 
No problem here if I close le first valve before opening the second one.

@justinmaiuto thank you for the report. Can you please  capture a debug log ([instructions](https://www.home-assistant.io/docs/configuration/troubleshooting/#enabling-debug-logging)) of this issue happening?

Generally, there are two things here:
(1) yes rainbird can't handle concurrent requests from multiple things and will reject requests when they arrive at the same time. have had to work through instability in the past as a result of this
(2) the rainbird integration has to query a device after sending a command to check its latest state, otherwise it reverts back to old state for a very long time until the next poll.
but i have never seen any of these crash anything.


An aggressive retry would be unexpected, just normal retries to deal with (1). Having details from your logs showing the problem from the home assistant PoV would be very helpful.

Tagging with beta milestone while we investigate in case this is a problem with the new release since this is tagged as `core-2025.x.x (maybe)`

I misread the information in the report, untagging from beta milestone.

