I think the key here is that ive confirmed that with the HA integration disabled, a zone cycle completes as commanded via the rainbird app. As soon as the HA integration is enabled, neither the app nor the HA commanded cycles run the full duration. Seems the nunber of requests is overloading the wifi LNK module causing it to restart, and the default behaviour after restart is to stop zone that is running. The potential linkage i see to the other issues being raised is im too seeing the zones go offline every now and then (though not coinciding with when zone irrigations stop short). But perhaps the device going offline is another symptom of an overloaded/restarting LNK module.

